<title>JAPAN: Sumitomo Metal to boost first-half copper output.</title>
<headline>Sumitomo Metal to boost first-half copper output.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sumitomo Metal Mining Co said on Wednesday it planned to boost its 1997/98 first-half refined copper production by 5.4 percent to 111,000 tonnes from the previous six months.</p>
<p>Sumitomo's scheduled output for the first half of fiscal 1997/98 and the schedules for the first and second half-years in 1996/97 were as follows (in tonnes per month, except for gold and silver in kilograms per month):</p>
<p>		   H1-1997/98	H2-1996/97	 H1-1996/97</p>
<p> Refined copper 111,000	   105,300	   105,300</p>
<p> Refined nickel  15,000	    14,000	    13,900</p>
<p> Ferro-nickel     9,600	     9,600	     9,600</p>
<p> Zinc		54,800	    52,300	    39,500</p>
<p> Gold (kg)	 12,100	    13,000	    13,300</p>
<p> Silver (kg)    119,700	   114,800	   113,800</p>
<p>Figures include production on a tolling basis.</p>
<p>No figures for actual output in 1996/97 were immediately available.</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodity Desk +81-3-3432-6179</p>
